                      "content": "⇧M is the first entry, only when write access allows it. Its title is the way forward, as the item's button says: “Merge…”, “Update branch”, “Resolve on GitHub” or “Mark ready…”; here the branch must be brought up to date first. Ordinary commands appear when they apply; here, a branch that's behind and a failed check that isn't required. The item menu (M2) and right-click (L2) title it the same way; theirs read “Merge…” as nothing comes first.",
