                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "bx80b",
                      "name": "Caption note",
                      "fill": "$fg-2",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Only what is tracked, grouped by owner (your own first, then organisations, then owners you aren't a member of), alphabetical inside a group. No ticks. Owners on the left, the same column as the picker (T18), with tracked counts; choosing one filters the list to it. Under it, \"Missing an organisation?\" with Grant access on GitHub, which opens GitHub's page for githq (github.com/settings/connections/applications/<client id>, getApprovalUrl), where an organisation githq can't see is granted (owner) or requested (member). Once granted, the organisation appears on the next read of the lists. A row opens that repository's settings (T16) on click or Enter, which the chevron says. Untrack sits on the row, shown on the hovered or selected row, ⌫ from the keyboard; it acts at once, with Undo (T20). Adding is a separate step: Track repositories (A) opens the picker (T18); a group's Track more opens it filtered to that owner, and is hidden when the owner has nothing left to track or can't be listed. Keys: J and K move, Enter opens, ⌫ untracks, A tracks more, 1 to 4 switch sections. While the lists are first read the tracked rows already show, since they come from what this browser keeps.",
