              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Beside the graph on the right (the tabs layout), always there on a wide window; below about 1200 px it folds away and B opens it over the graph. Every branch and tag on GitHub, the default branch first, then branches and tags newest first, each with its pull request and CI where it has them. B puts the cursor in its filter; typing narrows both groups; ↵ or a click scrolls the graph to the commit and selects it there. The graph is never narrowed to one branch.",
